  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arbitration Council Foundation 2019-2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Arbitration Council Foundation 2019-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pursuant to the proposal submitted by ACF dated on the 08 September 2022 to Sida, the proposed objectives for the following periods from 2023-2025 have been updated to previous objectives which are assessed timely relevant to the current labor context in Cambodia. The main objective of the contribution focuses on the &quot;Contribution to higher productivity, labour sector stability, and better living conditions for workers&quot;  with the following sub-objectives to achieve target results. 

1. Improved social dialogue and labour relations through accessible, transparent, and well-functioning labour dispute resolution system.

2. Increased participation and capacity of industrial relations beneficiaries in dispute prevention and resolution processes in selected enterprises and at the Arbitration Council.

3. Enhanced institutional integrity and sustainability of the Arbitration Council, Arbitration Council Foundation and their services.

4. Gender equality awareness is raised among ACF staff, Secretariat officials, Arbitrators, and ACFs beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">K&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;det till Arbitration Council Foundation f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra programmet &quot;Strengthening Industrial Relations and Labour Market Conditions in Cambodia&quot; varar under perioden 2019-2024. Den f&#xf6;reslagna insatsen syftar till att st&#xe4;rka industriella relationer och arbetsmarknadsvillkor genom social dialog och ett v&#xe4;lfungerande, trov&#xe4;rdigt skiljedomssystem f&#xf6;r arbetstvister i Kambodja genom 1) tvistl&#xf6;sning, 2) partnerskap och upps&#xf6;kande verksamhet med intressenter, 3) &#xf6;kad institutionell integritet och trov&#xe4;rdighet, och 4) institutionell kapacitetsst&#xe4;rkning och samarbete med arbetsministeriet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The core support to Arbitration Council Foundation  to carry out the Programme &quot;Strengthening Industrial Relations and Labour Market Conditions in Cambodia&quot; lasts for a period from 2019-2024. The proposed intervention aims at strengthening industrial relations and labour market conditions through social dialogue and well-functioning, credible labour dispute arbitration system in Cambodia by 1) labour dispute resolution, 2) partnership and outreach with stakeholders, 3) increased institutional integrity and credibility, and 4) institutional strengthening and collaboration with the Ministry of Labour and Vocational Training.</narrative>
  </description>
